* Week 10: ARRAY(n) / ARRAY(n, init) and indexing, A<I> (research/
* snobol/02-language-reference.md, "Arrays and tables"). Omitting the
* initial value defaults every element to the null string.
        A = ARRAY(5)
        A<1> = 10
        A<2> = 20
        A<3> = 30
        OUTPUT = 'A<1>=' A<1> ' A<2>=' A<2> ' A<3>=' A<3>
        OUTPUT = 'UNSET A<4>=[' A<4> ']'
* ARRAY(n, init) fills every element with init up front instead.
        B = ARRAY(3, 'X')
        OUTPUT = 'B<1>=' B<1> ' B<2>=' B<2> ' B<3>=' B<3>
* An out-of-bounds reference fails rather than crashing [GreenBook1971
* SS1.12] -- exactly like a failed pattern match or division by zero,
* this is a genuine SNOBOL4-level failure a goto field can react to.
        C = ARRAY(3)
        C<7>                                         :S(BADIDX)
        OUTPUT = 'OUT-OF-BOUNDS READ CORRECTLY FAILED'
* This subset is 1-based (an implementation choice, not a sourced
* fact -- the research corpus doesn't state a base), so index 0 is
* also out of bounds.
        C<0>                                         :S(BADIDX)
        OUTPUT = 'ZERO INDEX CORRECTLY FAILED (1-BASED)'          :(END)
BADIDX    OUTPUT = 'UNREACHABLE (OUT-OF-BOUNDS)'
END       N = N
